# Pre-existing finding (NOT introduced by NEARS-2986; regression_bugs lane, non-blocking)

Admin/app/Traits/PlaceNewOrder.php, new_place_order(), unchanged by this diff (confirmed via
`git diff abf27ae29 HEAD -- Admin/app/Traits/PlaceNewOrder.php` — this hunk does not appear):

    } catch (\Exception $exception) {
        info([$exception->getFile(), $exception->getLine(), $exception->getMessage()]);
        DB::rollBack();
        return response()->json(['errors' => [['code' => 'order', 'message' => translate('messages.failed_to_place_order')]]], 403);
    }

Matches active review-lessons.json rule `tx-guard-catch-exception-not-throwable` [low]:
a DB::beginTransaction()/lockForUpdate() guard must catch \Throwable, not \Exception — a PHP
\Error (TypeError, null method-call, DivisionByZeroError) thrown between beginTransaction() and
commit() escapes catch(\Exception), so DB::rollBack() is skipped and the transaction (plus this
flow's coupon-row FOR UPDATE lock) stays open on the connection. Pre-existing before this ticket;
flagged here since QA's own coverage of this exact transaction body surfaced it directly.
